  <prompt>Rename the "Promote" action to "Set related record", move it to the per-row overflow menu, and make it file an otherwise-unassociated analysis via a prompt: (a) associate to an existing matter/project (sets `regarding`), or (b) create/attach a Document to anchor it (regarding = document). Under the hood, name + create the sprk_analysis anchor + bind the session via the existing promote endpoint.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Full-stack (.NET 8 BFF + React/Fluent v9) expertise; comfortable with ADR-024 polymorphic regarding semantics and reusing the existing promote endpoint without adding a new one.</role>
  <goal>The prompt offers existing-record vs create-document; a filed session appears on the target matter's Analyses tab; an already-associated session does not offer the action (or shows its Analysis instead).</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-D9 (was "Promote") — the promote action files an otherwise-unassociated analysis. Server: AnalysisEndpoints POST /promote (:77-83; PromoteSession :1285-1403, already-associated guard at :1326-1330) → ChatSessionManager.PromoteSessionToAnalysisAsync:499-544. The client action moves into the 037 per-row overflow menu, replacing the old up-arrow promote dialog handler in HistoryOverlay.tsx.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/HistoryOverlay.tsx (the action moves into the 037 overflow menu; replace the old promote dialog handler)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs (PromoteSession:1285-1403)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs (PromoteSessionToAnalysisAsync:499-544)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">The association uses the polymorphic `regarding` field-set.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse the existing promote endpoint — do NOT add a new one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">An already-associated session must NOT offer the action (guard exists at PromoteSession:1326-1330).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r2/spec.md</file>
