  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Client: rename the action to "Set related record" in the 037 overflow menu; add the existing-vs-create-document prompt.</step>
    <step order="2">Path (a): associate to an existing matter/project (regarding). Path (b): create/attach a Document (regarding=document).</step>
    <step order="3">Wire both through the existing promote endpoint (name+create sprk_analysis anchor + bind).</step>
    <step order="4">Ensure already-associated sessions don't offer the action.</step>
    <step order="5">Build client + dotnet build; tests.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the promote endpoint cannot express the 'attach to existing document' path without a new endpoint, STOP and escalate (compose invariant: no new dispatch/endpoint) rather than adding one.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Set related record">
      <steps>From a history row overflow menu, choose Set related record, verify the existing-vs-create-document prompt; file to a matter; verify it appears on the matter's Analyses tab; verify an already-associated session doesn't offer it. Include an ADR-021 dark-mode check.</steps>
      <expected>The prompt offers existing-record vs create-document; the filed session appears on the matter's Analyses tab; an already-associated session does not offer the action; no dark-mode regressions.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <outputs>
